WEBVTT

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.220
Let's see...

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.700
What should I do with these?

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.810
I might as well have some fun...

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:21.560
Huh?

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.060
What's up, Yuuji?

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.440
I hear they're gonna host something.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.170
Host something?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.240
Fumizuki Academy sponsored...

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.460
Treasure Hunting...

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.020
Orienteering Competition?!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.850
Something that grows when its alone, What is it?

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.130
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.510
Never, Never give up!

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.810
One more chance, One more chance!

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.110
Never give up!

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.240
Meeting with someone else is easy

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.010
I decided what to say before they even asked

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.620
My heart beats fast thinking if I passed or not

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.800
I can't panic in this fight for love

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.870
Study! Study! Study! Keeps me up all night

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.500
I've got a dreaming genius inside me

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.080
I'd be great if everyone's wishes came true

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.250
I won't care about other people's lives

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.210
Perfect-area complete!

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.840
I'll definitely be waiting for you!

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:33.240
I can hear your voice from the Perfect-area!

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.550
Ah! Ear! Ear!

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.820
Why? Why can't stop when I pass you

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.430
if I'm your counselor

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.020
"Are we friends?" Yes, we're friends."

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.020
But, I failed the test with a 0

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:48.330
No! I'll take it again! and again!

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.470
I'm serious. One more chance, please

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:54.940
There's something better for is in the future

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:01.030
Better than my life right now.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.790
Fifth Period
Maps and Treasures and Striker Sigma V

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.720
Akihisa Yoshii has found some gold.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.710
Man, I haven't eaten like this in forever.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.080
It all looks so good!

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.340
Fumizuki Flour is every bit as delicious as I thought it would be.

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.170
Tastes just like bread!

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.590
I'd have no complaints if I could just get some jam...

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.510
You have no room to complain in the first place.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.020
I guess flour digests pretty quickly...

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.820
Fox Phi. Kisaragi Land's mascot character.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:41.380
Welcome

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.110
By the way, it's very popular with the kids.
Welcome

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.720
Isn't this Kisara-

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.370
I already explained it in the narration.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.660
Whoever lost this is probably looking for it right now.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.510
I guess I'll just leave it here.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.530
I can't find it... I can't find it...!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.020
Morning, Hazuki.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.600
What are you doing here?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.330
Oh! Good morning, Mr. Stupid!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.500
I'm looking for something I lost.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.100
Lost?

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.640
I lost my Phi strap.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.100
It's a limited edition... They don't sell it anymore.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.970
Oh, that? It's right over-

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.660
Jesus, what now!?

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.280
Phi!

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.240
What's the matter, Yoshii?

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.590
Mr. Fukuhara!

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.330
Great timing!

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:31.740
Gimme permission to do a summon!

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:36.920
Why, exactly?

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.130
It's an emergency! Just hurry up!

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:43.180
I guess I might as well. Just remember, this is an exception.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.020
All right!

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.150
Summoning Being...

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.170
Summon!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.640
All righty! Grab that strap!

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.050
Save Phi!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.050
Are you okay, Yoshii?

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.030
Mr. Stupid!

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.330
Christ... That damn feedback system...

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.370
What the hell is your problem?

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:19.130
Good morning, Mrs. Principal.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.340
You scared the hell outta me!

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.840
Don't use Beings to wreak havoc like that!

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.190
I wasn't!

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.050
I just wanted to pick that strap up...

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.770
This is why you shouldn't be playing with toys.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.780
Hey, you don't have to put it like that!

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.190
Your summoning permission has been suspended.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.690
Beings are absolutely not to be used for violent purposes.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.920
Violent!? I was just doing that for-

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.710
Summoned Beings are not toys for idiots!

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.800
Are you frustrated? Why not try proving that you're not an idiot, then?

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:15.850
You might just be able to get your hands on what you want, too.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.780
Sorry, Hazuki...

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:22.310
It's okay...

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:24.490
Hazuki...

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.030
So that's what the principal meant.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.030
The prizes are written here.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:34.410
Free meals for a year!?

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.370
Coupons for new video games!?

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.750
Sounds pretty awesome.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.250
It also mentions "secret items"...

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:45.710
A Phi-Noin-Ain limited edition strap set?!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.260
The hell, Akihisa?

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.830
I want this! This! This! This!

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.730
Why on Earth do you want that?

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:50.880
Who cares?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.390
So how do we win those prizes?

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.390
This is a map of the school grounds.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.220
We're gonna search for them using this?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.730
Not to brag, but I'm awesome at finding treasure in RPGs.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.770
And these are the test questions.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:03.880
What?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.660
The answers to the questions on these represent the coordinates for the checkpoints.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.610
We then exchange tickets for prizes at said checkpoints.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.800
That means...

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.070
We can't get 'em if we don't answer the questions correctly?!

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.740
It's also first-come, first-serve.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.010
If you run into another team,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.710
you have to settle it with a Summoning Battle.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.460
I'm being cockblocked by everything!

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.380
Wait a sec... I just need to get on a team with Himeji!

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.050
Back to your seats.

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.090
I'm gonna announce the teams for the orienteering competition.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.670
Who's in my team...?

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:33.930
Yuuji and Hideyoshi!?

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:37.100
Himeji and Minami are in a team with Voyeur!?

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.070
I grouped all of the troublemakers together.

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.480
I don't even want to know what you guys have in mind.

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.280
Hey, that's not exactly fair!

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.090
Hideyoshi is cute, so whatever...

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.000
but Yuuji is completely useless!

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.400
And you're not?

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.910
You have the entire school day to search.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.920
This is no laughing matter!

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.370
So take it seriously.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.650
There are three questions in each set, huh?

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.700
The answer to the first one is the x coordinate.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.480
Y coordinate for the second.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.330
And z for the third.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.510
Or, in layman's terms, which floor it's on.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:14.010
Hey, check this out! They're all multiple choice.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.830
This'll be a snap.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.010
You're good at multiple choice?

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.150
How can you not know my specialties?

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.810
Whatever. Get a load of this!

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.850
Man, I almost believed you for a second, too...

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.480
For math, I use the Striker Sigma V!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.020
For modern Japanese, I use the Problem Breaker!

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.820
And Shining Answer for history!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.010
They're all accurate beyond belief.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:40.160
Do you always just leave things to chance?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.410
Don't treat them lightly!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.240
Just watch.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.640
Do I have to?

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:48.040
Roar, Striker Sigma V!

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.130
All right!

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.590
I got the answer!

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.230
X coordinate: 652.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:07:59.510
Y coordinate: 237.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.970
Z coordinate: 5.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:06.390
Target locked on! It's over there!

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.650
Wow, it's floating.

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.910
Go fetch it.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:11.310
This is weird.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.350
Did they make a mistake writing the problems?

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.520
It's your fault, dumbass.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:16.700
Found it!

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.650
Awesome! It's a prize ticket.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.340
Looks like we drew first blood.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:25.450
Hooray!

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.420
It looks like our x and y were correct, at least.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.650
I told you! Striker Sigma V is awesome.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.710
You're more "amazing" for actually believing it works.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.100
We can redeem this for a year's worth of free desserts!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.010
Let's split them between us.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.390
I'll pass.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:42.030
Are you on a diet?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:45.320
I'll take this if we manage to find it, though.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:48.430
A premium ticket to Kisaragi Grand Park?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.060
Oh, I see! You want to go with your boyfriend!

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.520
No, he's my husband.

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.920
I just felt a chill down my spine.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.990
You have my sympathy.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.950
I can't answer anything besides math!

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.930
You're pretty smart, Tsuchiya...

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:06.320
I skipped everything except health.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.400
Ignored

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.480
Done!

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.230
Wow! Let's go there!

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.710
These coordinates...

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:19.970
<b>Female Changing Room</b>

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:23.250
I get to walk into the girls' changing room legally...

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.670
Okay! Let's look for the prize!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.930
It's a changing room, sure...

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.600
but no one is changing!

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.810
Of course not.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:39.750
We need to tidy this place up...

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:42.440
We're not afraid of the guys seeing it, so it's pretty much a mess...

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:45.690
There's no reason to come here unless it's in use.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.620
What's wrong, Tsuchiya? Are you okay?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.670
I'm fine... This is nothing...

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.680
Tsuchiya!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.300
I won't lose here!

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.060
Tsuchiya!

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:21.490
Amen...

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.500
All right, let me take a look...

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.230
at how those idiots are doing.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:45.960
Pierce the heavens! Problem... BREAKER!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.090
The coordinates point to around here.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.220
Our classroom?

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.810
The hell is this?

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.340
Not the prize, at least.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:08.910
Weird... maybe I should try condensing it more?

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.940
Just cross out everything.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:13.150
Um, you found it?

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.320
This is yours?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:18.300
Yes, that basket...

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.740
Yoshii, uh...

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.300
What's up?

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.070
Do you like sweets?

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:26.080
Yeah, I love 'em!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:32.250
Thank goodness! Actually, I woke up early today to bake some chiffon cakes.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:35.700
Wow! I didn't know you could bake cakes.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:36.800
Uh, just a sec!

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:41.870
Nice work, Problem Breaker.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.100
You've struck gold.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.550
You were such a good guy.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.250
I'll never forget you.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.520
Don't act like I'm about to die...!

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.480
I think it'd be nice if you could all eat some of it.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:58.240
Here you go.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.050
There's four of you, so there's not enough to go around...

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.820
Three chiffon cakes. Four people.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:15.050
Only one of us will live to see tomorrow.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.650
Welcome to the first annual...

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.690
...power level competition!

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.470
We'll decide it with rock paper scissors!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.650
Yeah!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:35.070
This is a battle of life and death.

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.780
Mizuki and Tsuchiya are sure taking their sweet time...

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.070
What are they up to?

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:54.950
Dammit! One more problem and my head's gonna explode!

00:12:54.950 --> 00:12:56.640
Don't worry.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:57.490
Miharu?

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:58.810
I'm over here.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.380
I've solved them all!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.060
What are you doing?!

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:06.060
Please look at the answers I slaved over for you, Sissy!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:09.450
Once I compared the coordinates with the map,

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:15.520
I discovered that the prize was hidden in your bra!

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:19.450
Please prepare to surrender your body and soul to me.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:20.860
I'd rather die!

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.580
Just let go of me!

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:25.890
No way! The coordinates don't lie!

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:29.110
The Ministry of Education agrees! Don't even bother trying to argue!

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:30.410
You've made a mistake!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:35.460
Then let's make an even bigger mistake together.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:35.510
Together!

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.420
Hell no!

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:42.750
You know, if they have the time to host these damn things,

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:45.600
why don't they use it to accelerate the course material instead?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.810
The coordinates point to here.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:51.190
This is Yoshii's shoebox!

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.420
If someone sees me here...

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:58.980
They're going to think that I'm sneaking a love letter into Yoshii's shoebox!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:03.660
No, no. I'm just here to get my tickets.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:10.960
Wait a sec...! Won't it look like I'm stealing someone else's love letter to Yoshii?

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:15.000
No, no. I only want the treasure inside.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.330
I don't care what others think! I can do this!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:22.630
But wouldn't the contents of Yoshii's shoebox be considered a treasure by some!?

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.320
I'll never escape this guilt!

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:29.380
What... What should I do?!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.850
Does it matter?

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.870
Sparkle!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:35.770
Shining Answer!

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.110
There it is.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:41.120
You rock, Hideyoshi!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.860
I don't think I had much to do with it.

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:45.320
Let's see what the prize is.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:46.740
Failed?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.060
So this isn't what we were looking for.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:51.630
Dammit! They pulled one over on us!

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:54.210
How could random chance pull one over on us?

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.480
I need to change the angle of it...

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:59.340
I don't think that's going to increase the accuracy.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.820
All right.

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:01.690
What do you think?

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.950
You actually answered it!

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.420
Are you sure it's right, Yuuji?

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.850
I don't want to end up somewhere crazy because you screwed it up.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.810
Look who's talking.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.640
According to Yuuji's answer...

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.890
it should be here.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.560
Wow! There really is one!

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.080
How'd you manage to solve it?

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.360
I chose a set with problems that I could solve.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.900
Wow, you're pretty good.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.010
You're at the bottom of the class with regards to test scores, though...

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:25.730
You must've cheated!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.360
Is it really that hard to convince you?

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.870
So what's the prize?

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.050
Let's see...

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.910
A premium couples' ticket to Kisaragi Grand Park?

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:40.210
All couples are invited to participate in our mock-wedding event.

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.670
Sounds pretty cool.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.060
You should go with Kirishima.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.260
Don't even say that!

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.450
She'd turn that "mock" wedding into the real thing!

00:15:49.450 --> 00:15:51.910
Don't show me shit like that!

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.580
You two can go!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.270
Really?

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:57.940
Hideyoshi, are you free this Sunday?

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.070
The ticket says it's for couples!

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:03.950
No way! Do you hate me!?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.110
I'm a guy.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:07.370
I've been rejected!

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:09.280
Does God hate me or something?

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:13.540
There's only one thing I can do at this point...

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.530
Hideyoshi, I love you!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.590
What the hell!?

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.340
These words hold a deeper meaning!

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.990
You might not know this, but, in Japan,

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:24.510
there's a legend saying that you'll be blessed if you confess beneath a legendary tree!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.130
That's not a legend.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:29.280
And there's only one thing "legendary tree" could be referring to at this school...

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:32.470
It refers to the legendary beauty, Hideyoshi Kinoshita.

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:37.560
In other words, you'll be blessed if you confess to Hideyoshi!

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:39.480
What, Hideyoshi!?

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:39.990
Really? If that's true, we can all confess to Hideyoshi without fear of being persecuted!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:44.400
This is wrong on so many levels that I don't even know where to begin.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:46.190
I love you, Hideyoshi!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:51.770
Snap out of it!

00:16:53.890 --> 00:16:57.740
Well, looks like it's not gonna work out for us after all.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.470
This is pretty unfair for idiots like us.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:03.560
There aren't many prizes left.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.170
I wonder what the secret items are.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:09.620
The Phi straps are still available!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.860
You still haven't given up?

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:14.800
The only problems left are pretty fucking hard.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.430
Or are you just gonna walk around randomly?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.100
Randomly...

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.320
That's right! I'll just answer all of them!

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:26.240
What are you going to do?

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.570
I'm going to fill in every possible coordinate.

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:29.860
All of them?

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:35.530
There might be a prize at places where the x and y axes intersect!

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.960
What about the floor?

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.790
We'll just have to check all of them!

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.320
That's a lot of places to look through!

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.620
Do you know long this would take...?

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.300
This game is based around searching high and low.

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:46.170
That's crazy talk...

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.510
I see. That's pretty clever.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:53.390
No harm in trying. Not like we can solve the problems anyway!

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:54.970
We'll show them how idiots do things!

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:56.440
Yuuji...

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.230
I'll go to the fourth floor.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:02.750
Akihisa, you go to the third.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.200
Hideyoshi, you go to the second.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:04.610
Okay.

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:05.570
Roger that.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.570
The janitor's closet!

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:09.100
Nothing.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.360
Empty.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:10.900
Female changing room

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:10.930
Empty.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.210
Nothing.

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.200
None.

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:17.080
Occupied...

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:17.490
The lockers.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:20.040
Nothing.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:20.880
None.

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:21.500
A dog?

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:24.230
The changing rooms!

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.140
Trash cans.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:30.870
Nothing.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:31.440
None.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:32.890
W-Why?!

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.480
The women's bathroom!

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:35.330
Nothing.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.140
None.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:37.510
There's somebody in here.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.380
The fish tank.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:41.180
Nothing.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:41.880
None.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.200
Ouch!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.570
Once again!

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:45.460
Nothing.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:46.150
None.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:47.270
Let me go...

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.870
One more time!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:49.920
I'm using it.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:51.280
There's someone here.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:53.420
Thank god it's empty...

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.070
Or not!

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:56.000
Hi.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:04.220
Dammit, we didn't find shit.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:06.230
There's nowhere left to look.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.820
No, there's one place left!

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:13.130
There's nowhere you could hide stuff there, though.

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:15.110
No way...

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.490
No one's found the strap yet.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:18.760
It has to be hidden somewhere.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:26.070
Found it!

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.720
I knew it!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.230
Hideyoshi, you don't need to answer problems to-

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.900
Hmm? I found this place after solving all of the questions.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:36.450
You're...

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:39.100
Sister! Why are you here?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:45.120
The rules say that we can use a Summoning Battle to take that ticket by force.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.950
Don't tell me...

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.640
Permitted.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.000
Summon!

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.300
Summon.

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:00.920
This isn't good, Akihisa.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.650
They're way too strong for us.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:05.030
I didn't think we'd have to go up against them...

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.980
Shit... What should we do?

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.310
We're not going to go easy on you.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.310
Ready to get your asses kicked?

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.130
See ya later.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:19.630
What?

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.120
Time's up.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.550
That means...

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.010
You're right.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:25.370
Yup.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.360
Kisaragi Grand Park
mascot strap set exchange ticket

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:31.040
Yippee!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:35.910
Wow, look at these! There's three in a set, too!

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:37.010
That's great.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:39.540
Hazuki is gonna love this.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.690
What is this?

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:44.970
Are these the secret items?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.090
I wonder what these do.

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:48.810
There's a manual.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.690
Iron Bracelets. The activation phrase is "Awaken".

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:54.040
So...

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:55.400
What do they do?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.550
Let's try it out.

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.260
Awaken!

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.200
This is...

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.510
No way...

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.410
Summon!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.710
Wow!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:13.290
We can summon our Beings without a teacher's permission!

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:17.190
The range is kind of limited, but this is still pretty sweet!

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.180
Why am I the only one whose clothes got torn?

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:30.440
Akihisa, is yours okay?

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.030
Uh, yeah.

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:32.700
That means that only dumbasses can use these.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:34.370
Dumbass

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.690
What do you mean by that?!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.280
You're a dumbass too!

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.200
Then you're a super dumbass.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:39.320
Ultimate

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:39.580
What?

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:39.910
Fine, the ultimate dumbass.

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:40.470
What?

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:41.480
Fine, the ultimate dumbass.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:42.160
What?!

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:43.120
The dumbass to rule all dumbasses.

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:44.580
What do you mean by that?!

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.740
I see.

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:49.880
They're still getting there.

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:53.530
But...

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.090
Idiots are like scissors - it's all about how you use them.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:01.630
Every night turns to dawn, after all.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:19.670
Baka, go go home!

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:22.940
It's a time of peace now that school's out

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:24.490
If I were to compare her

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:26.030
"She's a real angel!"

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:29.000
Then a sudden note ruined my fun

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:30.390
It said I have a makeup test!

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:31.780
It's hell!

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:35.120
I was joking with my friends,

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:38.150
"There's no way someone is that stupid!"

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:41.230
But deep down inside,

00:22:41.230 --> 00:22:42.520
I was screaming,

00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:45.480
"That was me! I'm that stupid!"

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:52.060
I thought the "Monthly" sign in the parking lot

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:57.340
was the company's name!

00:22:57.340 --> 00:23:00.090
For the longest time...

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:03.790
Stupidity is a manly character

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:06.490
Is that our lack of common sense?

00:23:06.490 --> 00:23:09.800
Rules are useless in this world

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:12.800
Eat Korean BBQ every night and overthrow the masses!

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:14.440
Look!

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:19.010
The sun that rose from the west is now setting down.

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:22.050
Run! It's almost dinner time.

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:28.920
Let's go home!

00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:38.340
Question six:

00:23:38.340 --> 00:23:41.190
Please list the different types of medleys.

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:44.060
Anisong medley, oldies medley, pigeon cookies!

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:46.240
I like pigeon cookies myself.

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:48.500
Next episode: Me and Pool and Swimsuit Paradise and.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:50.450
This will be on the test.
